   "html_text": "On the other hand, Edmund Henden (2016) argues on phenomenological grounds that addiction should not be assimilated to weakness of will. Addiction often involves habitual behavior, and addicts may continue to take drugs even when they don’t find it pleasurable to do so. (For discussion of habitual weak-willed action from a different perspective, see Silver 2019.) Henden contends that in these respects addiction is profoundly unlike giving into temptation, as paradigm examples of akrasia are ofte",
